+  >= 1000 now renders differently (e.g. 1500 -> "1.5s", was "1500ms"), and
+  non-integer/non-number inputs that used to return strings now throw.
+  External callers could not be searched from this repo; human review of
+  downstream impact recommended.
+- Probes outside the repo (not Ticket evidence) matched the Approach at the
+  boundaries: 999->"999ms", 1000->"1s", 1099->"1s", 59999->"59.9s",
+  60000->"1m 0s", 3600000->"60m 0s"; -0 -> "0ms"; Infinity, 1.5, "1000",
+  null, undefined, 10n, new Number(5) -> TypeError.
